---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy"
  description="ControlCurrent has no accounts, analytics, browser fingerprinting, or server-side profile storage."
>
  <header class="shell page-header">
    <span class="eyebrow">Privacy by static architecture</span>
    <h1>Your browser baseline stays in your browser</h1>
    <p>
      The deployed application has no account, analytics, advertising, telemetry, production API, or
      application database.
    </p>
  </header>
  <article class="shell prose">
    <h2>Profile handling</h2>
    <p>
      A deployment profile is held in memory while the planner is open. It is written to one
      bounded, versioned <code>localStorage</code> key only when you choose “Save locally”. You can clear
      that value from the planner. Exported JSON is generated in the browser.
    </p>

    <h2>No browser detection</h2>
    <p>
      ControlCurrent does not read or retain the user-agent string, infer installed browser
      versions, enumerate browser capabilities, or fingerprint the visitor. Browser minimums are
      explicit inputs.
    </p>

    <h2>Offline evidence input</h2>
    <p>
      The offline inspector keeps pasted response headers in page memory only. It does not fetch a
      URL, persist the input, or include raw header values, cookie names, or cookie values in its
      report. Request credentials are refused. Redact secrets before pasting and use “Clear” when
      finished.
    </p>
    <p>
      Evidence bundles can also contain an opaque scope inventory, HTML, bounded local resource
      bytes, selected request headers, reduced WebAuthn configuration, and an expected-surface
      manifest. Markup is parsed without execution or resource loading. Inventory entries and
      resource bytes are reduced locally and omitted from reports. Reduced reports also omit
      exclusion reasons, HTML, resource locations, inline content, CSP nonces and hashes, request
      targets, credentials, cookie data, WebAuthn challenges, relying-party identifiers, user
      identifiers, and credential identifiers. Labels and opaque surface IDs remain in an export, as
      do reduced inventory kind, completeness, time, counts and fingerprint, surface requirements,
      application and environment IDs, revision, optional build ID, producer ID, capture timestamps,
      model provenance, and a SHA-256 fingerprint of the reduced report. The fingerprints do not
      authenticate the producer or prove inventory completeness by themselves. An optional CLI-only
      Sigstore verifier retains only its state and the bounded certificate issuer and URI identity
      after successful verification; it does not retain the complete bundle, certificate,
      transparency entry, or trust metadata. Keep every label, identifier, surface ID, and
      evidence-policy exception reason non-identifying.
    </p>

    <h2>Network boundary</h2>
    <p>
      Compatibility data ships with the static site. The Content Security Policy denies runtime
      connections, and the planner makes no fetch request. External documentation links use a
      no-referrer policy. Sigstore verification does not run in the browser and uses a hash-pinned
      packaged trust target without a network refresh.
    </p>
    <p>
      A separate opt-in CLI collector can make bounded requests to an exact authorised origin. It
      requires a private manifest, explicit confirmation, and private output path; follows only
      same-origin redirects; and sends no cookies or credentials. Target origins and paths remain in
      the private manifest rather than dedicated bundle fields, but captured headers and HTML can
      still contain locations. The raw bundle therefore remains private. The collector is not
      reachable from this website.
    </p>
    <p>
      ControlCurrent refuses interactive use when it detects an embedded frame. On a shared hosting
      origin, enter only deliberately redacted examples; use a dedicated reviewed origin before
      handling organisation-specific evidence.
    </p>

    <h2>Deletion</h2>
    <p>
      Use “Clear saved profile” in the planner or clear site storage in your browser. There is no
      server copy to request or delete.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
